  "scope": "Exact native C int count variant for existing owning bytes/text output. Negative values including INT_MIN use existing uint64/INT64_MAX admission rejection before payload/terminator reads, while consuming output blocks and preserving primary native errors. No new runtime helper, new syntax or contract-row growth.",
  "contractRowBytes": 28,
  "qualificationNotes": [
    "Generic signed fixture span spelling corrected from unsupported const unsigned char* to existing const uint8_t* after full compiler freeze; actual accepted root source hashes are pinned by gates. Production compiler/binding sources match both full build freezes.",
    "Diagnostic r1 compiled units succeeded, then rejected that fixture span spelling. Diagnostic r2 passed emit but redundantly supplied automatically discovered companion C. Corrected r3 on Windows and r2 Linux execute the actual current fixture; historical failures preserved externally.",
    "IR source overlays recompile sem/IR/Cgen over a complete pinned source parent, whose src diff has only six changed files and no layout change. They are source preflights, separate from complete O2 CLI/nested EXE/DSO acceptance.",
    "Other count descriptor spellings and incompatible signedness/rank pointer prototypes remain rejected; complete programs import no xlang/TCC compiler libraries."
  ]
